    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1231">

                <pb facs="1215" n="929" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg929"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.142/1602</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-24T15:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 24, 1916, 3 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 8 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1412. Your 1486, April 27. Foreign Office replies that Ministry of Marine regrets
                    that very serious military reasons which prevented acquiescing to American
                    Government’s previous request of a like nature already explained (see my
                    telegram 1344,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1231-f1"/> April 4, 7 p. m.) apply equally
                    to a vessel coming out of a blockaded port and returning immediately, as such
                    trip would allow a reconnaissance from <pb facs="1216" n="930" xml:id="pg930"/>
                    which the military and naval forces of the powers at war with France would not
                    fail to profit, whatever dispositions might be taken by the American Government
                    or the French naval authorities.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
